            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 89-year-old female patient, admitted on 24/03/2017 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Physical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests were obtained to exclude secondary pathology. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and received appropriate patient education regarding her condition and inhaler technique. Her clinical course was favourable with significant symptomatic improvement. She is discharged home in a stable condition under ICD-10 J44.1. Please continue maintenance bronchodilator therapy and ensure close outpatient follow-up. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
